## Project layout

The code under `src/{{ package_name }}/` is layered. Dependencies point inward: `api -> application -> domain`. `adapters` implement the interfaces in `application/ports.py`. These rules are enforced by import-linter (`.importlinter`, run by `make lint`).

### Source (`src/{{ package_name }}/`)

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `main.py` | Composition root: builds the FastAPI app and wires adapters into use cases. The only module allowed to import everything. |
| `config.py` | Typed settings. The only place that reads environment variables (see `.env.example`). |
| `observability.py` | Logging setup (structlog, JSON to stdout), called once at startup. |
| `api/` | HTTP transport only. Contains no business logic. |
| `api/routers/` | Route handlers (`health.py` is the example). They call use cases. |
| `api/schemas/` | Pydantic request and response models. They are part of the OpenAPI contract. |
| `api/errors.py` | Maps exceptions to RFC 9457 problem-details responses. The only place errors become HTTP responses. |
| `api/middleware.py` | Request-ID middleware, bound to every log line. |
| `application/` | Orchestration layer. Depends on the domain and on ports, never on adapters. |
| `application/use_cases/` | One module per business action. This is the entry point for both routers and AI tools. |
| `application/ports.py` | Interfaces (Protocols) for everything the app needs from the outside world. |
| `domain/` | Pure business logic. No I/O, no framework and no LLM imports. |
| `domain/models/` | Entities and value objects. |
| `domain/rules/` | Business rules and policies. |
| `domain/services/` | Domain logic that does not belong to a single model. |
| `domain/errors.py` | Typed domain errors. Raise these instead of returning error strings. |
| `adapters/` | Implementations of ports. All outbound I/O lives here. |
| `adapters/db/`, `queue/`, `storage/`, `keyvault/`, `http_clients/` | Database, messaging, blob storage, secrets and calls to other services. |
| `ai/agents/` | LLM agents. They never import `api/` or non-LLM adapters. |
| `ai/tools/` | Tools exposed to agents. They call use cases, never adapters. |
| `security/` | Authentication and authorization. |
| `common/` | Small technical helpers only. It imports nothing from this package and holds no business logic. |

Most of these packages are empty placeholders. Add code to the layer it belongs in rather than creating new top-level folders. A new layer or pattern needs an ADR.

### Repository root

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `tests/unit/`, `tests/integration/`, `tests/contract/` | Tests. Unit tests mirror `src/`. Contract tests check the code against `docs/api/openapi.yaml`. `tests/unit/architecture/` checks the layout. |
| `evals/` | Model evaluations (`make eval`, costs money). |
| `docs/api/openapi.yaml` | API contract. Change it first. `scripts/export_openapi.py` regenerates it. |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decision records (MADR). |
| `scripts/` | Repo checks used by `make check` and CI (commit message, ignore rules, agent config, OpenAPI export). |
| `.importlinter` | Layer dependency rules. Do not add exceptions to get a build passing. |
| `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `.python-version` | Dependencies and tool configuration (ruff, mypy, pytest). |
| `Makefile` | Entry points: `make install`, `run`, `check`, `test`, `security`. |
| `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore` | Container build. |
| `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml` | CI pipeline and local hooks. |
| `CODEOWNERS` | Required reviewers, including for security-sensitive and architecture files. |
| `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` | Instructions for AI coding agents. |
| `.claude/` | Claude Code settings, hooks and path-scoped rules. |
| `.gitlab/duo/` | GitLab Duo rules. Generated, do not edit by hand. |

